WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.560
One of the most intriguing aspects of Bird
Box is that we never actually see the creatures

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.110
that are terrorising the world, but if you
watch very carefully, we are given some crucial

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.789
little clues about them and who they've killed.

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:17.700
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing seven monstrous details

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.540
you may have missed when watching Netflix's
viral sensation Bird Box.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.340
Plus, I'll be revealing some brand new behind-the-scenes
photos of a monster that was designed for

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.050
the movie but never used.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.370
Spoilers ahead so take care if you haven't
seen the film yet.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:35.730
The first details of the monsters emerge after
everyone who's holed up inside Douglas's house

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.610
try to figure out what's going.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:42.540
But it's Charlie who probably has the best
insight into what humanity is now up against.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.610
He explains that what's happening is the end
game and he lists the names of various mythological

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.100
demons and malevolent religious entities that
he's been studying for a book he's writing.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.940
The "Aka Manah" that Charlie mentions is often
depicted as a horned entity and one of Gary's

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.739
sketches resembles the Zoroastrian demon.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:05.639
Aka Manah signifies "Evil Mind", "Evil Purpose",
"Evil Thinking", or "Evil Intention" which

00:01:05.639 --> 00:01:10.450
fits in nicely with how the monsters in Bird
Box take over the minds of people who see

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.450
them.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:15.299
Depictions of Aka Manah sometimes show him
manipulating people like they're puppets on

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:16.380
a string.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.299
He's a particularly cruel and intelligent
demon who, ultimately, seeks death for the

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:21.630
humans he controls.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.709
In a post-apocalyptic movie like Bird Box,
it's pretty much expected that many of the

00:01:26.709 --> 00:01:30.450
characters we meet will end up getting killed
off with a few exceptions.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.840
But some of the deaths in Bird Box are much
harder to spot than others, for example, you

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.820
probably didn't take in what happened to the
couple who ran out of Douglas's house to try

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.130
and rescue their children.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.639
"If you go outside, you'll die."

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:43.280
"My children are out there!"

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.280
"Move!"

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.630
"You won't make it to your children!"

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:50.719
Well, when Tom and co drive out to the supermarket,
their car passes over a number of dead bodies

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:51.719
in the street.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:57.029
There's a stomach-churning moment, when we
see the car about to roll over a corpse, followed

00:01:57.029 --> 00:01:59.979
by the sickening sound of bones crunching.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:04.060
And if you look at the close-up of that body
before the car hits, you'll see it's actually

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.750
the guy who left the house several days earlier
and behind him is his wife.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.830
The body that gets run over has the same blue
jacket, light top and beige trousers the guy

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.720
had on in Douglas's house and the body of
the woman behind him has the same cream and

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:22.000
pale-coloured clothing his wife was wearing,
including the little bit of lace at the base

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.060
of her top.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.010
There are some interesting details in Malorie's
paintings at the beginning of the movie that

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.010
hint at what's to come.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:33.110
One of the paintings seems to foreshadow the
monstrous apocalypse unfolding on the TV screen

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.200
behind Malorie.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.890
You need to look very closely, but there's
a deer with what may be a wolf behind it,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.030
but even more strikingly, there's some kind
of monster to its side.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.680
It looks like a huge serpent has opened its
jaws about to attack the deer, and on top

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.190
of that, the head of the snake seems to be
emerging from an even larger, whale-like mouth

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.540
that's about to snap up the both animals,
who seem oblivious to their fate.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.950
And if you look even closer, you can see what
appears to be the head of a large-beaked bird

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.440
in the trees behind the enormous beast.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.220
Obviously, the painting's open to interpretation,
but it makes me think of the final scenes

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.070
of the movie where Malorie is running through
the forest fleeing from this enormous malevolent

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:12.230
force chasing her through the trees.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:15.740
The wind seems almost like it could devour
Malorie and the children in this shot, just

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:19.930
like the monster in this painting is about
to swallow up the animals.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.850
Another sinister being that shows up in Gary's
drawings is Cthulhu, a Lovecraftian cosmic

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.120
entity that lives beneath the earth.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.290
His appearance in Bird Box is especially relevant
because in the mythos of Cthulhu, simply gazing

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.680
upon him will drive an ordinary human insane.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.569
It's said that he, and other alien beings
like him, exist at a level we humans simply

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:43.720
cannot comprehend, which is why even looking
at him would drive us to madness.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:49.090
HP Lovecraft's description of Cthulhu mentioned
"an octopus-like head whose face was a mass

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:53.790
of feelers, a scaly, rubbery-looking body"
and the picture in Gary's drawings definitely

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.430
fits that.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:59.880
Interestingly and fittingly for our movie,
Cthulhu has cult followers, similar to the

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.710
worshippers of the creatures in Bird Box.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.640
This group has been able to look upon the
monsters and, rather than killing themselves,

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.319
they feel enlightened.

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:11.290
The man who attacks Malorie on the boat tells
her that "everyone must look" and that "it

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.959
shall cleanse the world!"

00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:17.889
Gary and Fish Fingers, the possessed guy at
the supermarket, say how beautiful the creature

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:22.460
is, and they both fanatically use whatever
tricks they can to gain access to survivors

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.469
to convert them to their cause.

00:04:24.469 --> 00:04:29.430
The post-apocalyptic scenario of Bird Box
also ties in with the idea that many Cthulhu

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.761
cultists and believers have that when Cthulhu
and his fellow gods rise again, the human

00:04:33.761 --> 00:04:35.169
race will be destroyed.

00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:39.960
So, Cthulhu seems to be big inspiration for
Bird Box, even if there's an array of other

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.199
drawings and sketches that Gary lays out on
the coffee table confirming that the monsters

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:47.240
in the movie [likely] look different to different
people.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.789
By the way, I wonder if the reason Gary has
drawn so many different versions of the monsters

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:57.110
is because he has some kind of dissociative
identity disorder, aka multiple personality

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:02.110
disorder, or alternatively, he may have collected
them together from other people at the mental

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.110
institution.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.990
A book in Douglas's house that Malorie gets
interested in is by Giovanni Piranesi, an

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:13.189
Italian artist who was known for his atmospheric
etchings of imaginary prisons, which have

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:18.110
been a major influence on films such as Metropolis,
Blade Runner, and The Third Man, writers like

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.830
Edgar Allan Poe and Franz Kafka, and artists
including MC Escher.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:27.280
Similar to Piranesi's drawings, the monsters
in Bird Box create an imaginary prison in

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.870
the mind of their victims.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.809
Remember what Charlie said, that it's "the
entity that takes on a form of your worst

00:05:32.809 --> 00:05:36.050
fears or... your deepest sadness or your greatest
loss."

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:40.370
So, the monsters cut individuals off from
others, locking them away within their own

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.370
minds.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:45.199
In other words, they create a prison of fear,
sadness and loss inside people's heads which

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:48.599
nobody else can see or understand the true
horror of.

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:53.020
That eventually leads them to either suicide
or possession and control by the creatures

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.190
in the case of characters like Gary or Fish
Fingers.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.969
Malorie herself suffers from an emotional
disconnect with the rest of the world at the

00:05:59.969 --> 00:06:04.889
beginning of the movie, but she very gradually
connects with other people like Tom and, eventually,

00:06:04.889 --> 00:06:08.919
by the end, she breaks out of her own figurative
prison, connecting with the children she's

00:06:08.919 --> 00:06:11.150
raised and the community she's joined.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:16.139
A curious reference to another source of weird
and wonderful creatures comes via a book that

00:06:16.139 --> 00:06:20.370
Malorie grabs to read while Greg is trying
to observe the creatures via the security

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.569
camera footage.

00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:26.089
The book she's holding while talking to Charlie
is called "Cabinet of Natural Curiosities"

00:06:26.089 --> 00:06:29.469
by the 18th-century Dutch natural historian
Albertus Seba.

00:06:29.469 --> 00:06:34.629
And, appropriately enough, it's full of drawings
of real-life and mythical beasts, ranging

00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:39.379
from creatures of the deep to an array of
snakes and a creepy seven-headed hydra monster

00:06:39.379 --> 00:06:44.080
that's especially difficult to defeat as cutting
a head off the beast causes another two to

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.510
grow in its place.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:49.560
In my Alternate Ending and Deleted Scenes
video, I spoke about how the creatures were

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:54.039
originally going to appear in a scene in Bird
Box, and since making that video the special

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:58.830
effects makeup company KNB EFX have released
photos of what the creature would have looked

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.150
like during Malorie's deleted nightmare scene.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:06.189
These are some pictures shared on Instagram
by KNB EFX co-owner Howard Berger.

00:07:06.189 --> 00:07:09.559
On the left is the design for the prosthetic
piece for the monster.

00:07:09.559 --> 00:07:13.210
That was then placed on actor Dirk Rogers
and makeup applied on top.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.869
The final result is in the bottom right corner.

00:07:15.869 --> 00:07:20.389
This deleted scene was originally in the movie
because, according to screenwriter Eric Heisserer,

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:24.409
one of the producers was insisting that a
creature had to be shown at some point.

00:07:24.409 --> 00:07:28.240
Director Susanne Bier also explained that
although a lot of time and expense went into

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.069
filming the creature scene, when they reviewed
it they didn't feel it was scary enough.

00:07:32.069 --> 00:07:36.490
And with these new pictures we can see why
Sandra Bullock described the look of the creature

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.900
as "snake-like" and resembling "a long fat
baby".

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:43.430
I don't know if there were ever any plans
to add any additional CGI effects on top of

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.830
the creature in post-production to make it
more menacing.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:49.779
But I can see why this scene was cut in the
end as the real horror of the monsters in

00:07:49.779 --> 00:07:55.080
Bird Box is that they tap into each individual's
deepest fear, so by giving them a definitive

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.059
form, the scariness would be lost for many
viewers.

00:07:58.059 --> 00:08:01.680
And if you want to find out more about other
deleted scenes and the horrific alternate

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.469
ending to Bird Box that didn't make it into
the movie, you can tap in the top right for

00:08:05.469 --> 00:08:08.339
my video on that or check the links in the
video description.

